  "details": "I'm 26, children are annoying, and I neither need nor want to interact with ANYONE under 16 for ANY REASON (said 16 instead of 18 since there's some chill peeps that aren't as loud or cringe, might be the edge of a generation or something).\nThis can be SUPER HELPFUL in two ways- this can make it so adults like me doesn't have to interact with/see/hear ANYONE under [age], but ALSO so children can be... \"shielded\" to a degree from anyone that's considerably older than them, due to the rumors I've heard, even though I've only been on here for a week or so.\nSadly, this would mean age-verification or something, though there's easy ways to \"cheese\" it, like asking once what their birth year is, then locking it unless they open a support ticket asking for help. The options are there, conceptually it's really easy, but I understand that it might be harder to implement than I make it sound.",
